# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 2.5408e+03 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 0.8490 84.584 3.9983e+04 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~85 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 2.0700 62.336 2.7675e+06 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.08 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 F flare 2.0917 61.941 6.0872e+06 stylized  Light rises x5.2 in 0.12 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 62.3 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 61.5 km (99% of m0). Dust groups supply 29% of the rise and 24% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
5 B first_breakup 2.1146 61.525 1.2425e+07 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x4.5 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
6 P peak 3.3176 40.449 6.6218e+07 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+2.2 km from the peak of energy deposition (38.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 16.4 km/s).
7 b bump 3.3186 40.433 6.6217e+07 stylized  Small fluctuation, 6% above the local trend; no breakup within 0.1 s (overlap of several groups' light / pancake growth). The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
8 - drag_overtakes_ablation 3.6446 35.536 4.7865e+07 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
9 D rolloff 3.8696 32.656 2.4089e+07 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.55 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 64% of v0, 36% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
10 T tail 4.8446 25.576 6.5359e+04 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
11 R retirement_step 5.1056 24.648 7.0988e+03 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 54% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
